    "rationale": "SBP2 participates in recoding UGA for selenocysteine incorporation into selenoproteins. Thyroid hormone deiodinases are selenoproteins, so SECISBP2 deficiency reduces deiodinase activity and can produce relatively high T4, low T3, and nonsuppressed TSH without a primary thyroid synthetic defect. Strongest alternative resolved: THRB disease alters nuclear thyroid-hormone signaling and hypothalamic-pituitary feedback, but it does not explain biallelic SECISBP2 variants with directly reduced deiodinase activity. The demonstrated lesion is defective selenoprotein synthesis."
  }
